insert into nodes (node_type, slug, title, summary, status, meta_title, meta_description, legacy_slugs, published_at) values ('article', '100-best-things-to-do-in-the-maldives-an-ultimate-guide', '100 Best things to Do in the Maldives: An Ultimate Guide', 'Here', 'published', '100 Best things to Do in the Maldives: An Ultimate Guide | Maldives Travel Guide | MTG', 'Here', ARRAY['/articles/best-things-to-do-in-maldives.html']::text[], now()) on conflict (node_type, slug) do nothing;
insert into articles (id, body, reading_time_minutes) select id, '<h3>1. Snorkeling</h3><p>The Maldives offers some of the most spectacular snorkeling in the world. This is due to the abundance of coral reefs in the region, as well as extremely clear waters. There are, in fact, close to 70 distinct species of coral reefs and more than 700 species of marine life. This means when you snorkel here you are sure to see an amazing variety of flora and fauna. Just some of the species you are likely to see include reef sharks, various kinds of turtles, rays, napoleons and morays. Whether you are an expert on marine life or not, you can still appreciate the colorful array of creatures you will be able to observe. Snorkeling highly recommended thing to do in Maldives.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/snorkeling.webp" alt="Snorkeling" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>2. Diving</h3><p>The Maldives has become one of the world''s best scuba diving destinations because of the white sand beaches, coral reefs, clear warm waters, numerous scuba diving sites and rich marine life.</p><p>Most holiday resorts in the Maldives have a scuba diving facility and there are a number of liveaboard operators offering scuba diving cruise holidays that take guests to many dive sites all over the Maldives. Many scuba divers are keen to dive in the Maldives because of the presence of whale sharks, manta rays, eagle rays, reef sharks, hammerhead sharks and moray eels, as well as many smaller fish and coral species. Diving is one of the best thing to do in Maldives.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-diving.webp" alt="maldives diving" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>3. Stay in an Overwater Bungalow</h3><p>Experience luxury at its finest by staying in an overwater bungalow. Enjoy direct access to the ocean, stunning views, and the ultimate in privacy and comfort.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/resorts/over-water-room-maldives-w.webp" alt="over water room maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>4. Explore Male, the Capital City</h3><p><a href="/maldives/islands/male/">Male</a>, the bustling capital of the Maldives, offers a mix of modernity and tradition. Visit the markets, explore the local culture, and see the historical sites.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/maldives-capital-male-city.webp" alt="maldives capital male city" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>5. Swim with Manta Rays</h3><p>Join a guided tour and swim with these gentle giants. The Maldives is one of the best places in the world to encounter manta rays, especially around the Hanifaru Bay.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/manta-point-lankanfinolhu-island.webp" alt="Manta-Point-Lankanfinolhu-Island" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>6. Enjoy a Private Beach Dinner</h3><p>Treat yourself to a romantic dinner on a secluded beach. Many resorts offer this exclusive experience, complete with gourmet food and stunning sunset views.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/baros-island/images/baros-maldives-island-resort-beach-dinner.webp" alt="Private Beach Dinner" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>7. Visit a Traditional Maldivian Village</h3><p>Get a glimpse into the local way of life by visiting a traditional Maldivian village. Learn about the culture, customs, and daily activities of the islanders.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/local-island-tours.webp" alt="Traditional Maldivian Village" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>8. Take a Seaplane Tour Over the Atolls</h3><p>See the Maldives from above with a seaplane tour. The aerial view of the turquoise waters, coral reefs, and white-sand islands is breathtaking.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/transfers/maldives-seaplane-transfers.webp" alt="take a Seaplane Tour" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>9. Try Night Fishing</h3><p>Experience the traditional way of fishing in the Maldives by going on a night fishing trip. Catch your own fish and enjoy a barbecue under the stars.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/fishing/cast-fishing.webp" alt="try Night Fishing" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>10. Relax in an Underwater Spa</h3><p>Indulge in a unique spa experience at one of the Maldives'' underwater spas. Relax as you watch the marine life swim by through the glass walls.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/underwater-spa-maldives.webp" alt="Relax in an Underwater Spa" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>11. Experience a Sunset Cruise</h3><p>A sunset cruise is a perfect way to end your day in the Maldives. Watch the sky turn vibrant shades of orange and pink as the sun sets over the Indian Ocean.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-sunset-cruise.webp" alt="Experience a Sunset Cruise" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>12. Dine at an Underwater Restaurant</h3><p>For an unforgettable dining experience, visit an underwater restaurant. Enjoy gourmet cuisine while being surrounded by the ocean''s beauty.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/ozen-maadhoo-underwater-restaurant.webp" alt="Dine at an Underwater Restaurant" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>13. Visit a Sandbank</h3><p>Spend a day on a secluded sandbank surrounded by nothing but the azure ocean.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/sandbank-trip-in-maldives.webp" alt="Visit a Sandbank" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>14. Visit the Hukuru Miskiy (Friday Mosque)</h3><p>This ancient mosque, built in 1658, is a must-visit in Male. Its intricate coral stone architecture and wooden carvings make it a unique historical site.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/hukuru-miskiy-friday-mosque.webp" alt="Visit the Hukuru Miskiy (Friday Mosque)" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>15. Explore the Maldives Islamic Centre</h3><p>The Maldives Islamic Centre, with its golden dome, is an iconic landmark in Male. It serves as a center for religious and cultural activities.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-religion.webp" alt="Explore the Maldives Islamic Centre" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>16. Attend a Maldivian Cultural Show</h3><p>Experience the rich culture of the Maldives by attending a traditional music and dance performance. The bodu beru drums are a highlight of these shows.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-culture.webp" alt="Attend a Maldivian Cultural Show" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>17. Dive with Whale Sharks</h3><p>The Maldives is one of the few places where you can dive with whale sharks, the largest fish in the ocean. These gentle giants are often found around the South Ari Atoll.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/whale-shark-sighting.webp" alt="Dive with Whale Sharks" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>18. Participate in Coral Reef Conservation</h3><p>Join a coral reef conservation project and contribute to preserving the Maldives'' delicate marine ecosystem. Many resorts offer guest participation in coral planting programs.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/diving/meedhoo-coral-garden.webp" alt="Participate in Coral Reef Conservation" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>19. Kayak Through Mangroves</h3><p>Explore the unique mangrove forests of the Maldives by kayak. Paddle through narrow channels and observe the diverse flora and fauna.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/kayak-riding-maldives.webp" alt="Kayak Through Mangroves" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>20. Visit Vaadhoo Island for Bioluminescent Plankton</h3><p>Vaadhoo Island is famous for its bioluminescent plankton, which lights up the shoreline at night. This natural phenomenon is a mesmerizing sight.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/bioluminescent-beach-maldives.webp" alt="Visit Vaadhoo Island for Bioluminescent Plankton" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>21. Enjoy a Floating Breakfast in Your Villa</h3><p>Start your day with a luxurious floating breakfast in your private villa pool. This indulgent experience is offered by many of the Maldives'' top resorts.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/floating-breakfast-in-maldives.webp" alt="Enjoy a Floating Breakfast" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>22. Visit the National Museum in Male</h3><p>The National Museum in Male houses a collection of artifacts that tell the story of the Maldives'' rich history and culture. It''s a must-visit for history enthusiasts.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/maldives-national-museum.webp" alt="Visit the National Museum in Male" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>23. Go on a Dolphin Watching Tour</h3><p>The Maldives is home to several species of dolphins, and a dolphin watching tour is a great way to see them in their natural habitat. Watch as they playfully swim and jump alongside your boat.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/dolphin-cruise.webp" alt="Go on a Dolphin Watching Tour" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>24. Experience Traditional Maldivian Fishing</h3><p>Join local fishermen on a traditional fishing boat and learn the art of fishing the Maldivian way. This hands-on experience is both fun and educational.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/fishing/fishing-history-of-maldives.webp" alt="Experience Traditional Maldivian Fishingg" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>25. Indulge in a Luxury Spa Treatment</h3><p>Pamper yourself with a spa treatment in one of the Maldives'' many luxury resorts. From massages to facials, you''ll find a range of treatments to rejuvenate your body and mind.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/meeru-island/images/meeru-island-resort-spa.webp" alt="Indulge in a Luxury Spa Treatment" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>26. Watch the Sunrise from a Secluded Beach</h3><p>Rise early and head to a secluded beach to watch the sunrise. The tranquility and beauty of the morning light make it a peaceful start to the day.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/resorts/maldives-low-budget-resort.webp" alt="Watch the Sunrise from a Secluded Beach" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>27. Go Big Game Fishing</h3><p>For thrill-seekers, big game fishing is a must. Head out into the deep sea and try to catch marlin, tuna, and other large fish.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/fishing/big-game-fishing-maldives.webp" alt=" Go Big Game Fishing" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>28. Try Water Skiing</h3><p>The calm, warm waters of the Maldives are perfect for water skiing. Whether you''re a beginner or an expert, this activity offers thrills and fun.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/wakeboard-inmaldives.webp" alt="Try Water Skiing" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>29. Windsurfing in the Maldives</h3><p>With its warm waters and steady winds, the Maldives is an ideal place for windsurfing. Many resorts offer equipment and lessons for beginners.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/windsurfing-maldives.webp" alt="Windsurfing in the Maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>30. Explore Shipwrecks While Diving</h3><p>The Maldives is home to several shipwrecks that have become popular dive sites. Explore these underwater relics and the marine life that now inhabits them.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/maldives-diving-wrecks.webp" alt="Explore Shipwrecks While Diving" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>31. Go Parasailing Over the Indian Ocean</h3><p>Parasailing offers a bird''s-eye view of the Maldives'' stunning scenery. Soar above the islands and take in the panoramic views of the turquoise waters.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/parasailing-maldives.webp" alt="Go Parasailing Over the Indian Ocean" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>32. Enjoy a Beachfront Yoga Session</h3><p>Start your day with a peaceful beachfront yoga session. The serene surroundings and the sound of the waves create a perfect atmosphere for relaxation and mindfulness.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/conrad-rangali/images/conrad-maldives-rangali-island-resort-pool.webp" alt="Enjoy a Beachfront Yoga Session" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>33. Explore Local Markets in Male</h3><p>Discover the local way of life by visiting the bustling markets in Male. The fish market is especially lively, with fresh catches being sold daily.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-shopping.webp" alt="Explore Local Markets in Male" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>34. Enjoy a Family-Friendly Snorkeling Trip</h3><p>Take the whole family on a Maldives snorkeling adventure. The shallow lagoons of the Maldives are perfect for kids to explore the underwater world safely.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/snorkeling-in-maldives.webp" alt="Enjoy a Family-Friendly Snorkeling Trip" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>35. Take a Cooking Class in Maldivian Cuisine</h3><p>Learn how to prepare traditional Maldivian dishes by taking a cooking class. You''ll get hands-on experience with local ingredients and techniques.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/live-cooking-class-in-maldives.webp" alt="Take a Cooking Class in Maldivian Cuisine" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>36. Discover the Marine Life at a Research Center</h3><p>Visit a marine research center and learn about the efforts to protect the Maldives'' unique marine ecosystem. Some centers offer guided tours and educational programs.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/marine-life-in-the-maldives.webp" alt="Discover the Marine Life at a Research Center" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>37. Explore Male''s Historical Sites</h3><p>Discover the history of Male by visiting its historical sites, such as the Old Friday Mosque, the Sultan Park, and the Mulee Aage Palace.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/male-maldives.webp" alt="Explore Male''s Historical Sites " loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>38. Visit Utheemu Palace</h3><p>Utheemu Palace, located on Utheemu Island, is the birthplace of Sultan Mohamed Thakurufaanu, a hero in Maldivian history. The palace is now a museum.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/utheemu-ganduvaru.webp" alt="Visit Utheemu Palace" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>39. Experience a Full Moon Beach Party</h3><p>Join a full moon beach party, a popular event in the Maldives. Dance under the stars to live music and enjoy the vibrant atmosphere.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/park-hyatt/images/park-hyatt-maldives-hadahaa-reception.webp" alt="Experience a Full Moon Beach Party" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>40. Try Deep Sea Fishing</h3><p>Deep sea fishing in the Maldives is an exciting adventure. Head out into the open ocean and try your luck at catching big game fish like marlin, tuna, and sailfish.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/fishing/bottom-fishing-in-maldives.webp" alt="Try Deep Sea Fishing" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>41. Capture Stunning Photos on a Photography Tour</h3><p>Join a photography tour and capture the beauty of the Maldives through your lens. Whether you''re an amateur or a professional, the Maldives offers endless photo opportunities.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/hideaway-beach/images/hideaway-beach-resort-and-spa.webp" alt="Capture Stunning Photos on a Photography Tour" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>42. Take a Catamaran Sailing Trip</h3><p>Sail around the atolls on a catamaran and enjoy the stunning views of the Maldives from the water. Many trips include stops for snorkeling and swimming.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/catamaran-sailing-trip.webp" alt="Take a Catamaran Sailing Trip" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>43. Explore the Lhaviyani Atoll</h3><p>Lhaviyani Atoll is known for its pristine beaches and excellent diving spots. Explore this lesser-known atoll and discover its natural beauty.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maps/maldives-atoll-map.webp" alt="Explore the Lhaviyani Atoll" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>44. Watch a Movie Under the Stars</h3><p>Many resorts in the Maldives offer outdoor movie screenings on the beach. Enjoy a classic film while lounging on the sand under the night sky.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/beach-movie-screen-maldives.webp" alt="Watch a Movie Under the Stars" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>45. Experience Flyboarding</h3><p>Try the adrenaline-pumping activity of flyboarding in the Maldives. Hover above the water and perform tricks with the help of a water-powered jetpack.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/flyboard-maldives.webp" alt="Experience Flyboarding" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>46. Visit the Maldives Fish Market</h3><p>Pamper yourself with a traditional Maldivian spa treatment. Many resorts offer massages and therapies using local ingredients like coconut oil and seaweed.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male-fish-market-maldives.webp" alt="Visit the Maldives Fish Market" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>47. Explore the Artificial Beach in Male</h3><p>The Artificial Beach in Male is a popular spot for locals and tourists alike. It''s a great place to swim, relax, and enjoy the vibrant atmosphere.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/male-city-beach.webp" alt="Explore the Artificial Beach in Male" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>48. Relax in a Lagoon-View Jacuzzi</h3><p>Unwind in a jacuzzi with a view of the lagoon. Many resorts offer private jacuzzis where you can relax and soak in the stunning surroundings.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/relax-in-a-lagoon-view-jacuzzi.webp" alt="Relax in a Lagoon-View Jacuzzi" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>49. Try Kitesurfing</h3><p>Kitesurfing is a thrilling activity that combines surfing and kite flying. The Maldives'' steady winds and clear waters make it an ideal destination for kitesurfing enthusiasts.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-kitesurfing.webp" alt="Try Kitesurfing" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>50. Take a Speedboat Tour</h3><p>Explore the atolls on a speedboat tour. These tours are fast-paced and exciting, offering a different perspective of the Maldives'' beautiful islands.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/transfers/maldives-speed-boat-transfers.webp" alt="Take a Speedboat Tour" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>51. Visit a Sea Turtle Rehabilitation Center</h3><p>Learn about sea turtle conservation efforts by visiting a rehabilitation center. These centers rescue and care for injured turtles before releasing them back into the wild.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/sea-turtle-rehabilitation-center.webp" alt="Visit a Sea Turtle Rehabilitation Center" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>52. Learn to Surf in the Maldives</h3><p>The Maldives is an excellent destination for both beginner and experienced surfers. Many resorts offer surfing lessons, and the waves are perfect for riding.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/surfing-maldives.webp" alt="Learn to Surf in the Maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>53. Explore the Maldivian Wildlife</h3><p>The Maldives is home to a variety of wildlife, including tropical birds, flying foxes, and geckos. Take a nature walk and discover the islands'' unique flora and fauna.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/day-tours-to-villages.webp" alt="Explore the Maldivian Wildlife" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>54. Scuba Diving at Banana Reef</h3><p>One of the most famous dive sites in the Maldives, Banana Reef is known for its stunning coral formations and diverse marine life. Dive into the deep blue and discover a world teeming with life.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/diving/maldives-dive-site.webp" alt="Scuba Diving at Banana Reef" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>55. Join a Guided Island Hopping Tour</h3><p>Discover the diversity of the Maldives by joining a guided island hopping tour. Each island has its own unique charm, from luxury resorts to local villages.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/islandhop.webp" alt="Join a Guided Island Hopping Tour" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>56. Participate in a Marine Biology Workshop</h3><p>Many resorts offer marine biology workshops where you can learn about the unique marine life of the Maldives and the importance of conservation.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/diving/divemaster-course.webp" alt="Participate in a Marine Biology Workshop" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>57. Experience Glamping on a Private Island</h3><p>Combine luxury and adventure by glamping on a private island. Enjoy the comforts of a luxury tent while being surrounded by nature.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/resorts/child-friendly-island-resorts-maldives.webp" alt="Experience Glamping on a Private Island" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>58. Visit a Maldivian Souvenir Shop</h3><p>Buy local handicrafts and souvenirs to take home.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-shopping.webp" alt="Visit a Maldivian Souvenir Shop" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>59. Try Wakeboarding</h3><p>Wakeboarding is a thrilling water sport that involves riding a board while being towed behind a boat. The Maldives'' calm waters make it an ideal spot for beginners and experts alike.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/wakeboard-inmaldives.webp" alt="Try Wakeboarding" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>60. Visit a Sustainable Resort</h3><p>Stay at a sustainable resort and learn about the eco-friendly practices used to protect the environment. These resorts often offer educational programs and activities.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/resorts/best-budget-resort-maldives.webp" alt="Visit a Sustainable Resort" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>61. Explore the Southernmost Atolls</h3><p>The southernmost atolls of the Maldives, such as Addu Atoll, offer a unique experience with their own culture, history, and natural beauty. Explore these less-visited islands for a more off-the-beaten-path adventure.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maps/maldives-map.webp" alt="Explore the Southernmost Atol" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>62. Try Stand-Up Paddleboarding</h3><p>Stand-up paddleboarding (SUP) is a fun and relaxing way to explore the calm lagoons of the Maldives. Paddle at your own pace and enjoy the beautiful surroundings.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/standup-paddleboarding-maldives.webp" alt="Try Stand-Up Paddleboarding" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>63. Visit the Maldives Whale Submarine</h3><p>The Maldives Whale Submarine offers a unique underwater experience for those who prefer to stay dry. Take a dive and explore the coral reefs without getting wet.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/tours/maldives-whalesubmarine.webp" alt="Visit the Maldives Whale Submarine" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>64. Attend a Local Festival</h3><p>Experience the vibrant culture of the Maldives by attending a local festival. Festivals like Eid and the Independence Day celebrations are marked with traditional music, dance, and feasts.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-eid-festival.webp" alt="Attend a Local Festival" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>65. Take a Jet Ski Safari</h3><p>A jet ski safari is an exhilarating way to explore the Maldives'' islands and atolls. Speed across the water and discover hidden coves and secluded beaches.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/jet-ski-riding-in-maldives.webp" alt="Take a Jet Ski Safari" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>66. Visit the Maldives Victory Wreck</h3><p>The Maldives Victory Wreck is a popular dive site for experienced divers. The shipwreck, which sank in 1981, is now home to a variety of marine life and coral formations.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/alif-alif-fesdhoo-wreck-maldives.webp" alt="Visit the Maldives Victory Wreck" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>66. Experience the Maldives'' Nightlife</h3><p>While the Maldives is known for its tranquility, there are still opportunities to enjoy the nightlife. Many resorts offer beach parties, live music, and themed events.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-nightlife.webp" alt="Experience the Maldives'' Nightlife" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>67. Take a Sunset Photo Tour</h3><p>Capture the beauty of the Maldives'' sunsets with a guided photo tour. Learn tips and techniques from a professional photographer while exploring the islands.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-sunset-photoshoot.webp" alt="Take a Sunset Photo Tour" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>68. Visit a Local School</h3><p>Visit a local school and learn about the Maldivian education system. This is a great way to interact with local children and understand their way of life.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-school.webp" alt="Visit a Local Schoolg" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>69. Relax on the Beach</h3><p>Sometimes the best thing to do in the Maldives is simply to relax on the beach. With miles of white sand and crystal-clear water, you''ll find your perfect spot to unwind.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/relax-on-the-maldives-beach.webp" alt="Relax on the Beach   " loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>70. Explore Hidden Lagoons by Canoe</h3><p>Discover the Maldives'' hidden lagoons by canoe. Paddle through serene waters and explore the tranquil beauty of the islands.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/explore-hidden-lagoons-by-canoe.webp" alt="Explore Hidden Lagoons by Canoe" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>71. Sky Dive Maldives Ifuru</h3><p>Tandem skydiving is a thrilling activity in which a willing person is paired with an accomplished skydiving instructor. Joined at the hip, they ride an aircraft to frightening heights and then jump out into the wide sky. An exhilarating rush of adrenaline and breath-taking panoramic views combine to create an incredible sensory explosion as they freefall at speeds of up to 120 mph. When the teacher opens the parachute, there''s a peaceful descent and a victorious landing. Unmatched excitement for individuals looking for a memorable, risk-free skydiving introduction.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/sky-diving-maldives.webp" alt="Sky Dive Maldives Ifuru" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>72. Visit the National Art Gallery in Male</h3><p>The National Art Gallery in Male showcases the work of local artists and provides insight into the Maldives'' vibrant art scene.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldivian-craftsmanship.webp" alt="Visit the National Art Gallery in Male" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>73. Discover the Maldives'' Blue Holes</h3><p>Dive into these underwater sinkholes for a unique Maldives diving experience, exploring their depths and encountering diverse marine life.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/diving/fushi-kandu-maldives.webp" alt="Discover the Maldives'' Blue Holes" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>74. Stay at Underwater Hotel</h3><p>The Conrad Maldives Rangali Island resort''s THE MURAKA is a unique luxury two-story home with a master bedroom submerged in the Indian Ocean over 16 feet below sea level.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/the-muraka-underwater-villa-maldives.webp" alt="Stay at Underwater Hotel" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>75. Experience a Traditional Maldivian Tea Ceremony</h3><p>Join a traditional Maldivian tea ceremony and sample local teas and snacks. This cultural experience is a great way to learn about Maldivian hospitality.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/traditional-maldivian-tea-ceremony.webp" alt="Experience a Traditional Maldivian Tea Ceremony" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>76. Relax in an Overwater Hammock</h3><p>Unwind in a hammock suspended over the water. Many overwater villas in the Maldives feature hammocks where you can relax and enjoy the ocean breeze.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/overwater-hammock-in-maldives.webp" alt="Relax in an Overwater Hammock" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>77. Visit the Tsunami Monument in Male</h3><p>The Tsunami Monument in Male commemorates the victims of the 2004 Indian Ocean tsunami. It''s a poignant reminder of the power of nature.</p><h3>78. Go Paddleboarding in the Crystal-Clear Waters</h3><p>Paddleboarding is a fun and relaxing way to explore the Maldives'' calm waters. Many resorts offer paddleboards for guests to use.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/paddleboarding-in-maldives.webp" alt="Go Paddleboarding in the Crystal-Clear Waters" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>79. Attend a Maldivian Wedding Ceremony</h3><p>Witness a traditional Maldivian wedding ceremony, complete with local music, dance, and customs. Some resorts offer packages for couples to renew their vows in this unique way.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldivian-wedding-ceremony.webp" alt="Attend a Maldivian Wedding Ceremony" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>80. Ride a Dhoni (Traditional Maldivian Boat)</h3><p>Sail the waters of the Maldives on a dhoni, a traditional wooden boat used by local fishermen. It''s a great way to experience the local way of life.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/traditional-maldivian-boat.webp" alt="Ride a Dhoni (Traditional Maldivian Boat)" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>81. Take a Semi-Submarine Tour</h3><p>Explore the underwater world without getting wet by taking a semi-submarine tour. These tours allow you to see the coral reefs and marine life from the comfort of a dry cabin.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/semi-submarine-tour-maldives.webp" alt="Take a Semi-Submarine Tour" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>82. Attend a Traditional Maldivian Dance Performance</h3><p>Experience the rhythm and energy of a traditional Maldivian dance performance. The bodu beru drums are a highlight of these shows.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/traditional-maldivian-dance-performance.webp" alt="Attend a Traditional Maldivian Dance Performance" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>83. Tour the Southern Atolls by Bicycle</h3><p>Explore the southern atolls of the Maldives by bicycle. Ride through local villages, along the coast, and through lush vegetation.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/best-things-to-do-in-maldives.webp" alt="Best-things to do in maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>84. Experience a Beach BBQ</h3><p>Enjoy a beach barbecue with freshly caught seafood and local dishes. Many resorts offer this dining experience as part of their all-inclusive packages.</p><h3>85. Take a Day Trip to Hulhumale</h3><p>Hulhumale is a reclaimed island near Male that offers a mix of modernity and natural beauty. Explore its beaches, parks, and local markets on a day trip.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/hulhumale-city-maldives.webp" alt="Take a Day Trip to Hulhumale" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>86. Fun Tubing</h3><p>Isn''t the name intriguing enough on its own? We don''t think anyone needs more reasons to like this pastime-the word &quot;fun&quot; is right in the name. Fun tubing, in contrast to many other water sports in the Maldives, involves climbing into an inflatable, unpowered tube that will shoot you through the water quickly. The rocky ride you''ll have on the lake is the best part. We assure you that it is definitely worth the effort. Among the best things to do on the ocean in the Maldives is this.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/fun-tubing.webp" alt="Fun Tubing" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>87. Try Underwater Photography</h3><p>Capture the beauty of the coral reefs and marine life with an underwater camera.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/diving/padi-scuba-diver.webp" alt="Try Underwater Photography" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>88. Banana Boating</h3><p>This fun activity involves speeding across the deep blue oceans of the ocean while strapped into a large boat to prevent you from falling over. In the Maldives, this heart-pounding team exercise is a must-do. So, minions, eat a banana a day to stave off holiday hunger!</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/explore-hidden-lagoons-by-canoe.webp" alt="Banana Boating" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>89. Take a Walking Tour of Male</h3><p>Discover the capital city of Male on a walking tour. Visit landmarks such as the Maldives Islamic Centre, the National Museum, and the fish market.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/male-city-guided-tour.webp" alt="Take a Walking Tour of Male" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>90. Day Visit to Resorts</h3><p>One of the most popular attractions in the Maldives are the overwater villas that have direct access to the sea. All I can say is that it''s one of the nicest things to do in the Maldives and a wonderful experience to stay in one. The rooms are huge, with the most plush beds; a sundeck, plunge pool, and jacuzzi are located at the rear of the apartment. All that is audible is the sound of the breeze and the water. Moreover, the vista is magnificent.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/day-visit-to-resort.webp" alt="Day Visit to Resorts" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>91. Virgin Islands Excursion</h3><p>Go to a desolate island in the Maldives for food and festivities after catching a great catch. Enjoy the wildness of nature all around you, take leisurely strolls along immaculate beaches, and go swimming in crystal-clear waters when the entire island is yours to yourself.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities/virgin-islands-excursion.webp" alt="Virgin Islands Excursion" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>92. Stingray Feeding</h3><p>Hundreds of stingrays gather in Male fish market jetty daily, and visitors can buy baitfishes and feed them.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/male-island-tour.webp" alt="Stingray Feeding" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>93. Experience the Maldives'' Local Cuisine</h3><p>Maldivian cuisine is a reflection of the country''s rich cultural heritage and its close relationship with the sea. The food is characterized by the use of fresh ingredients, particularly fish, coconut, and rice, which are staples in the Maldivian diet.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/maldives-island-resort-dinner.webp" alt="Experience the Maldives'' Local Cuisine" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>94. Explore the Maldives'' Underwater Caves</h3><p>The Maldives is not only known for its stunning overwater scenery but also for its fascinating underwater landscapes. Among these are the mysterious underwater caves, which offer a unique and thrilling diving experience. These caves, formed over thousands of years, provide a habitat for a diverse range of marine life and are a must-visit for experienced divers looking for adventure.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/diving/maldives-dive-site.webp" alt="Explore the Maldives'' Underwater Caves" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>95. Go on a Manta Ray Safari</h3><p>Join a guided safari to snorkel or dive with manta rays in their natural habitat, often during feeding or cleaning sessions.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/diving/addu-manta-point.webp" alt="Go on a Manta Ray Safari" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>96. Experience Scuba Diving at Night</h3><p>Discover the nocturnal marine life and the vibrant coral reefs after dark, illuminated by your dive torch.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/diving/alimatha-jetty.webp" alt="Experience Scuba Diving at Night" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>97. Go on a Whale Watching Tour</h3><p>Spot whales migrating through the waters of the Maldives, with the possibility of seeing species like blue whales and sperm whales.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/blue-whale.webp" alt="Go on a Whale Watching Tour" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>98. Take a Private Yacht Cruise</h3><p>Enjoy a luxurious day on the water with a customized itinerary, including stops at secluded beaches and snorkel spots.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/private-yacht-cruise.webp" alt="Take a Private Yacht Cruise" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>99. Explore the Thilafushi Island</h3><p>Known as the "garbage island," Thilafushi offers a unique insight into waste management and the environmental challenges faced by the Maldives.</p><h3>100. Visit the Hanifaru Bay</h3><p>Snorkel in this UNESCO Biosphere Reserve, famous for its large gatherings of manta rays and whale sharks.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/activities-to-do-in-maldives.webp" alt="activities to do in maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure>', 18 from nodes where node_type = 'article' and slug = '100-best-things-to-do-in-the-maldives-an-ultimate-guide' on conflict (id) do update set body = excluded.body, reading_time_minutes = excluded.reading_time_minutes;
